    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0291" n="207" xml:id="pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d143-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-10-22">22 October 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 632, Personal and Top Secret, from the President to the Prime
                    Minister.</p>
                <p>Your 795,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d143-f2"/> 796,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d143-f3"/>
                        797,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d143-f4"/> 799,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d143-f5"/>
                        800<anchor n="2" xml:id="d143-f6"/> and 801<anchor n="3" xml:id="d143-f7"/>
                    received.</p>
                <p>I am delighted to learn of your success at Moscow in making progress toward a
                    compromise solution of the Polish problem.</p>
                <p>When and if a solution is arrived at, I should like to be consulted as to the
                    advisability from this point of view of delaying its publication for about two
                    weeks. You will understand.</p>
                <p>Everything is going well here at the present time.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
